      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2012 Société française d\u2019anesthésie et de réanimation (Sfar). Published by Elsevier SAS. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "We reported the case of a 61-year-old woman, who has been hospitalized in ICU because of an extensive mesenteric ischaemia, involving the small bowel, secondary to a naratriptan overuse. This mesenteric ischaemia was complicated by multiple organ failure and was responsible for extensive small bowel resection and left colectomy. A concomitant abundant absorption of grapefruit juice, a well-known P450 inhibitor, may have enhanced this naratriptan toxicity. This case underscore that an abdominal pain occurring in the context of headache treatment may be related to a mesenteric ischaemia."
      },
